---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="Techversation has no accounts and no tracking. Your progress and theme choice stay in your browser." page="privacy">
  <main id="main" class="wrap page-narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem)">Privacy</h1>
    <p>Techversation has no accounts, no advertising and no analytics at the moment. This page says what the site does so you can decide for yourself.</p>
    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>Your color theme and the modules you mark as done are saved in your browser's local storage. They are never sent to a server. Clearing your browser data removes them.</p>
    <h2>YouTube</h2>
    <p>A video loads from YouTube only after you press play, using the privacy-enhanced player (youtube-nocookie.com). From then on YouTube's own terms and privacy policy apply to that video.</p>
    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>The site's fonts load from Google Fonts, so your browser contacts Google when a page opens. The fonts will be served from this site in a later version.</p>
    <h2>Requesting a course</h2>
    <p>The request form does not send anything itself. It opens your email app with the request written out, and you choose whether to send it. If you add your email address, it is only used to reply.</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If analytics or accounts are added later, this page will say so first.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
